  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns 480. I worked it out by hand and got the same result when I ran it.\n\n1. `service2.py` only imports `pricing.base_fee` and `discounts.apply_discount`. `decoy_tax.py` and `decoy_shipping.py` aren't used.\n2. `base_fee(1000)` gives 500 + 1000 // 10 = **600**.\n3. `apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` applies the gold rate of 20%: 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = **480**.\n\nANSWER: 480",
